{
 "result": "maze.py is a pure-stdlib BFS. It reads stdin as bytes, pads rows to a rectangle with a '#' border, and flattens the grid into one bytearray of visited cells. It expands by level with plain lists, exits as soon as E is discovered, and prints -1 when no path exists. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78), and the assay was accepted with a stable baseline of 3.23108 (noise 10.3%). I am resting rather than spending more energy on variants, since this level-list BFS is already close to the practical limit for pure Python and a further win would need to beat the baseline by more than the 10.3% noise.",
